%N A398271 Array read by antidiagonals: T(n,k) is the number of minimum feedback vertex sets in the grid graph P_n X P_k.
%C A398271 Also, the number of maximum induced acyclic subgraphs in the same graphs.
%H A398271 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A398271/b398271.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..496</a> (first 31 antidiagonals)
%H A398271 Giedrius Alkauskas, <a href="https://klevas.mif.vu.lt/~alkauskas/math/square-sequence-alkauskas.pdf">Maximal subsets of n X n board without cycles</a>, 2022.
%H A398271 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FeedbackVertexSet.html">Feedback Vertex Set</a>.
%H A398271 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GridGraph.html">Grid Graph</a>.
%F A398271 T(n,k) = T(k,n).
%F A398271 T(n,1) = 1.
%F A398271 T(2*n,2) = (n + 1)*2^n; T(2*n+1,2) = 2^n.
%F A398271 T(4*n,3) = (3*n + 1)*(3*n^2 + 9*n + 4)*2^(n-2); T(4*n+1,3) = 2^n; T(4*n+2) = (3*n+2)*2^n; T(4*n+3) = (9*n^2 + 25*n + 20)*2^(n-1).
%F A398271 T(n,4) = 8*n + 16 for n >= 6.
